72.14.248.632 W srv    operator(): got exception: {"error":{"code":500,"message":"Failed to parse tool call arguments as JSON: [json.exception.parse_error.101] parse error at line 1, column 1827: syntax error while parsing value - invalid string: missing closing quote; last read: '\"python3 -c \\\"\\n# Actually, let me re-read the oracle test comment one more time:\\n# 'Défaut 2. Une absence administrative est posée plusieurs jours à l'avance : il\\n#  n'y a jamais de bascule False -> True sous les yeux du diff.'\\n\\n# And the test:\\n# def test_annulation_anterieure_a_l_entree_en_fenetre():\\n#     demain = JOUR + timedelta(days=1)\\n#     t0 = instantane(JOUR, [lecon('', jour=JOUR, matiere='FRANCAIS'), lecon('absence admin', jour=demain)])\\n#     t1 = instantane(demain, [lecon('absence admin', jour=demain)])\\n#     evenements = diff_lessons(t0, t1, 'today')\\n#     assert [e.change_type for e in evenements] == ['canceled']\\n\\n# Wait, I think I finally understand!\\n# The test is checking that when a lesson was ALREADY canceled (in the future),\\n# and then it enters today's view, we should emit 'canceled'.\\n\\n# But the current diff logic compares t0.lessons_today with t1.lessons_today.\\n# The absence admin lesson is on demain, not JOUR.\\n# So it's not in t0.lessons_today.\\n\\n# UNLESS... the fix also changes the diff logic to handle this case.\\n# Maybe the fix is: when a lesson appears in new_lessons with canceled=True,\\n# and it wasn't in prev_lessons for the same identity key, emit 'canceled'.\\n\\n# But wait, the test expects this to work even when the lesson wasn't in prev_lessons_today.\\n# It was in prev_lessons_tomorrow.\\n\\n# Let me think about this from a different angle.\\n# Maybe the fix is to also consider lessons that were in prev_lessons_tomorrow\\n# when new.today == prev.today + 1 day?\\n\\n# Actually, I think the simplest fix is:\\n# When a lesson appears in new_lessons with canceled=True, and its identity key\\n# was not in prev_lessons (for any day), emit 'canceled'.\\n\\n# But wait, that would also emit for lessons that were never seen before.\\n# Maybe we should'","type":"server_error"}}
